2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - **Java records** (Java 16+): final classes with auto-generated canonical constructor, `equals`, `hashCode`, `toString`, and private-final components. Records cannot extend classes other than `Object`, cannot have extra instance fields beyond declared components, but can have any methods.
   - **`static final class` → `record` conversion**: The dominant refactoring pattern. Applicable when: (a) all fields are already immutable, (b) the class holds only those fields, (c) the class has no superclass, (d) other structurally identical types in the same file already use `record`.
   - **`--enable-preview --release 21`**: Required for compilation due to unnamed variable (`_`) syntax used elsewhere in the codebase. Pre-existing `ClassWriter: Position UNKNOWN in type annotation: @NonNull` warnings are noise.
   - **Iterator.remove() default**: `Iterator.remove()` already throws `UnsupportedOperationException` by default in Java, so explicit overrides that only do that are redundant.
   - **Dead code removal + inlining**: Commented-out debug trace blocks and intermediate variables used only once.
   - **Gradle multi-module project**: Unbuildable here (no network/cached deps); verify via `javac` on individual files.

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`src/main/java/io/reactivex/rxjava4/internal/functions/Functions.java`** (Refactoring #1)
     - 675-line utility class. Most inner adapters already used `record`. Four `static final class` types converted.
     - `Array5Func` was the only non-record in the Array2–Array9 series.
     - `ToMapKeySelector`, `ToMapKeyValueSelector`, `ToMultimapKeyValueSelector` converted.
     - Example conversion:
       ```java
       // Before
       static final class Array5Func<T1, T2, T3, T4, T5, R> implements Function<Object[], R> {
           private final Function5<T1, T2, T3, T4, T5, R> f;
           Array5Func(Function5<T1, T2, T3, T4, T5, R> f) { this.f = f; }
           @SuppressWarnings("unchecked")
           @Override
           public R apply(Object[] a) throws Throwable { ... }
       }
       // After
       record Array5Func<T1, T2, T3, T4, T5, R>(Function5<T1, T2, T3, T4, T5, R> f) implements Function<Object[], R> {
           @SuppressWarnings("unchecked")
           @Override
           public R apply(Object[] a) throws Throwable { ... }
       }
       ```

   - **`src/main/java/io/reactivex/rxjava4/internal/operators/observable/ObservableInternalHelper.java`** (Refactoring #2)
     - Already had 9 record types; 4 `static final class` types converted: `FlatMapWithCombinerInner`, `FlatMapWithCombinerOuter`, `FlatMapIntoIterable`, `ReplaySupplier`.
